#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Production-grade MBP deployment for enmaas-mini (Darwin + Podman machine).

Platform dispatch:
  - Linux/RHEL: delegate to scripts/pricetag/install.py (Quadlet, RHEL-only)
  - Darwin (MBP, applehv 10 vCPU / 16 GiB / 93 GiB Fedora 41 VM; M4 Pro 14 core 48 GiB host):
    compose-native path that reuses prepare.py logic (postgres_bootstrap, gateway render)
    but emits compose.laptop.yaml and runs via podman-compose.

Stack on Darwin/MBP (podman machine):
  - postgres:17.8 (placeholder for hardened registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16)
  - maas-api standalone arm64 build (M1/M2/M3/M4 - linux/arm64)
  - pricetag metering
  - praxis gateway (standalone)
  - llm-katan (mock/echo fixture via tests/common/provider.py)

Six stages (mirrors install.py 1-6):
  1. Validate provider setup
  2. Prepare host
  3. Acquire application images (platform-aware amd64/arm64)
  4. Import images
  5. Configure providers, TLS and budgets
  6. Start and verify services

Lifecycle:
  deploy --from-scratch  -> idempotent DB init, secrets, health, admin user
  deploy --verify        -> harness + benchmark (20 requests, exact ledger)
  teardown --purge-volumes -> compose down, volume/network rm, admin dirs

Usage examples:
  scripts/laptop/deploy --mode mock --hostname localhost --monthly-usd 5
  scripts/laptop/deploy --mode mock --hostname localhost --demo-fixture --from-scratch
  scripts/laptop/deploy --mode mock --hostname localhost --with-llm-katan --llm-katan-backend echo --verify --yes
  scripts/laptop/deploy --mode mock --hostname localhost --with-llm-katan --llm-katan-backend echo --from-scratch
  scripts/laptop/deploy --plan
  sudo scripts/laptop/deploy --mode real --provider openai --openai-key-file /root/openai.key
"""
